# The Dockerfile copies by explicit pattern (*.html, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, images/,
# nginx/), so nothing here is load-bearing for what ends up in the web root. It exists to
# keep the build context small, which is most of what `docker compose build` spends its
# time on given images/ is ~16 MB.
#
# NOTE: nginx/ must NOT be listed. The Dockerfile copies the two .conf files out of it
# into /etc/nginx, and a .dockerignore entry would make those COPY lines fail.

# The camera originals and the full-size Vinted downloads. The Dockerfile only ever copies
# images/derived/, so these were never IN the image — but they were still in the build
# CONTEXT, which the daemon tars up and ships on every single build. At 3 photos across 150
# listings that is ~240 MB of pointless copying per deploy, and it grows with the closet.
# The derived/ subdirectory is untouched by these patterns.
images/*.jpg
images/*.jpeg
images/*.JPG
images/*.JPEG

# Product data: read at build time by the scripts, never served.
data

# Local-only inventory view, deliberately never deployed.
inventory.html

# Mounted into the tunnel container as a read-only volume, never copied into the image.
.cloudflared

# Host-side machinery: the launchd watchdog and its logs.
scripts

.git
.gitignore
.claude
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Project notes, not site content.
*.md

Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
